	"FriendlyName": "LumaSwarm - Animated Light Swarms on a Budget",
	"Description": "Runtime scheduler for hundreds to thousands of animated dynamic lights. A single world subsystem drives flicker, pulse, strobe and colour-cycle animations for every registered light, sorts them into distance tiers, and writes at most a fixed number of lights per frame. MegaLights made the GPU side affordable; LumaSwarm is the authoring and budgeting layer for the CPU side.",
